{"id": "tea:jabala-upanisad:1", "source": "src:jabala-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1"}, "paraphrase": "Bṛhaspati asks Yājñavalkya about Kurukṣetra, the gods' place of sacrifice; it is Avimukta, the sacred place of Brahman; there Rudra teaches the tāraka to the departing life-breath, by which one becomes immortal. One should never leave Avimukta.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion", "knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["death-dying", "karma-liberation"], "concepts": ["cpt:avimukta-taraka"], "teachers": ["tch:brhaspati", "tch:yajnavalkya"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:jabala-upanisad:2", "source": "src:jabala-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "2"}, "paraphrase": "Atri asks where the infinite unmanifest Self is established: in Avimukta, which lies between Varaṇā and Nāsī — Varaṇā wards off the faults of the senses, Nāsī destroys them; it is the junction of the brows and nose, where the knowers of Brahman worship at the twilights.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["ultimate", "body-layers"], "concepts": ["cpt:avimukta-taraka", "cpt:inner-tirthas"], "teachers": ["tch:atri"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:jabala-upanisad:3", "source": "src:jabala-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "3"}, "paraphrase": "By reciting the Śatarudrīya one gains immortality; these are the names of immortality.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ritual", "naya": null, "path": ["sound", "ritual"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["sound-language", "karma-liberation"], "practices": ["prc:satarudriya-japa"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:jabala-upanisad:4-rite", "source": "src:jabala-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "4 (rite)"}, "paraphrase": "Some perform the Prājāpatya sacrifice, but one should perform the Āgneyī; fire is prāṇa. One smells the fire with 'this is your proper womb…'; if there is no fire, one offers into water, for water is all the gods.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ritual", "naya": null, "path": ["ritual"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["practice"], "concepts": ["cpt:sannyasa-rite"], "practices": ["prc:sannyasa-diksa"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:jabala-upanisad:4-stages", "source": "src:jabala-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "4 (stages)"}, "paraphrase": "Janaka asks about renunciation: having completed studentship one may become householder, then forest-dweller, then renounce; or else one may renounce directly from studentship, the household or the forest; whether under vows or not, with or without fires, 'on the very day one becomes dispassionate, on that day one should renounce'.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ethical-social", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ethics", "karma-liberation", "dispute"], "original": {"text": "yad ahar eva virajet tad ahar eva pravrajet", "script": "IAST", "edition": "Īśādiviṃśottaraśatopaniṣadaḥ (Nirṇayasāgara collection of 120 Upaniṣads), South Indian recension carrying Upaniṣad Brahmayogin's opening maṅgala verses; e-text github.com/sanskrit/raw_etexts vedaH/misc/upaniShat/mixedPF/108_Upanishads.md", "licence": "text public domain; e-text licence unstated"}, "concepts": ["cpt:sannyasa"], "teachers": ["tch:janaka", "tch:yajnavalkya"], "disputes": ["dsp:when-to-renounce"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:jabala-upanisad:5-modes-of-death", "source": "src:jabala-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "5 (modes of death)"}, "paraphrase": "The text allows the renouncer certain modes of ending life (the hero's path, abstaining from food, entering water or fire, the great journey). Recorded summary-only; no guidance is given here.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ritual", "naya": null, "path": ["ritual"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["death-dying"], "concepts": ["cpt:renouncer-permitted-deaths"], "restricted": true, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:jabala-upanisad:5-the-wanderer", "source": "src:jabala-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "5 (the wanderer)"}, "paraphrase": "The wanderer wears discoloured cloth, is shaven, without possessions, pure, harming none, living on alms, and becomes Brahman; if sick he renounces by mind and speech.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ethical-social", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["ethics", "karma-liberation"], "concepts": ["cpt:atura-krama-sannyasa", "cpt:renunciant-marks"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:jabala-upanisad:5-thread", "source": "src:jabala-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "5 (thread)"}, "paraphrase": "Atri asks how one without the sacred thread can be a brāhmaṇa; Yājñavalkya: the Self is his sacred thread; he sips water — that is the rule for wandering ascetics.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["ethics", "ultimate"], "concepts": ["cpt:inner-sikha-yajnopavita"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:jabala-upanisad:6-abandoning-marks", "source": "src:jabala-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "6 (abandoning marks)"}, "paraphrase": "Casting triple staff, water-pot, sling, bowl, strainer, topknot and thread into water with 'bhūḥ svāhā', naked, using the belly as bowl, he lives in empty houses, temples, grass huts, anthills, at tree-roots, in potters' sheds, fire-halls, sandbanks and caves, devoted to pure meditation, and abandons the body through renunciation.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ethical-social", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["ethics", "practice", "death-dying"], "concepts": ["cpt:renunciant-marks", "cpt:avadhuta"], "practices": ["prc:parivrajya"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:jabala-upanisad:6-paramahamsas", "source": "src:jabala-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "6 (paramahaṃsas)"}, "paraphrase": "Paramahaṃsas such as Saṃvartaka, Āruṇi, Śvetaketu, Durvāsas, Ṛbhu, Nidāgha, Jaḍabharata, Dattātreya and Raivataka had unmanifest marks and unmanifest conduct; not mad, they behaved as if mad.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "absolute", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "realized"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission", "karma-liberation"], "concepts": ["cpt:avadhuta", "cpt:renunciant-marks"], "teachers": ["tch:samvartaka", "tch:uddalaka-aruni", "tch:svetaketu", "tch:durvasas", "tch:rbhu", "tch:nidagha", "tch:jadabharata", "tch:dattatreya", "tch:raivataka"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
